<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39921" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quā^drum</span></b> , i, n.
		quattuor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>something square</i>, <i>a
			square</i>, <i>quadrate</i> (class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perticae dolantur in quadrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 3, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per quadrum singulos habens cubitos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Exod. 37, 25</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a being
			squared</i> or <i>fitted together</i>, <i>fitness</i>, <i>proper order</i>, <i>arrangement</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in quadrum redigere sententias,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Or. 61, 208</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">70, 233</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
